void *func_001449A8(s32); void func_003021B0(void*,s32,s32);
typedef struct { u8 pad_00[0x9A8]; s64 unk9A8; } TmpBig;
void *func_002EB790(void){ TmpBig *p=func_001449A8(0xA08); if(p==NULL) return p; func_003021B0(p,0,0xA08); p->unk9A8=0x28; return p; }
NOTES: (1) The early-return form ("if (ptr==NULL) return ptr; ... return ptr;") is required: the plain "if (ptr!=NULL){...} return ptr;" form produces a wrong branch-target layout (0x38 vs 0x3c, score 20). (2) Layout/count/operands are exact; only the li scratch reg differs. Tried without effect ($v0 every time): early-return, explicit return in both branches, void* ptr + cast, TmpBig* return type, long/u64 field, sizeof(TmpBig) struct of 0xA08, extra local copies, ternary/comma. Target materializes 0x28 into $v1 (addiu $v1,$zero,0x28; sd $v1,0x9a8($s0)). Suspect the original has an extra live value in $v0 (or a different allocator state). Info from caller func_002EB0F8: return value is a 32-bit pointer stored into fields 0x14/0x18 of the caller's object (sw), alloc size 0xA08, field zeroed by func_003021B0 (=memset).

Arrow/entity descriptor init: a->unk0 = D_00478188 (name str 'firearrow'); a->unk4 = 0; a->unk8 = 8; a->unkC = 0x1E (u16, sh); a->unk60 = D_00451400 (144 bytes data ptr). Store order in ROM: 0xC, 0x8, 0x60, 0x0, delay: 0x4. Best attempt (score 30, ONE displaced instruction, struct: u8*unk0, s32 unk4, s32 unk8, u16 unkC @0xC, pad, u8* unk60 @0x60): source exactly
  a->unkC = 0x1E; a->unk8 = 8; a->unk60 = D_00451400; a->unk0 = D_00478188; a->unk4 = 0;
Mine emits lui a1,lui a2, [lo a1, lo a2, addiu v0=0x1E, addiu v1=8]; ROM wants lui a1,lui a2, addiu v0=0x1E, lo a1, lo a2, addiu v1=8. I.e. gcc hoists the two lui's (found: try declaring D_00451400 as s32[] and fields as u8* gives this) and everything else matches. Only the addiu $v0,$zero,0x1e lands one slot late. Tried: statement orders C/8/60/0/4, C/60/0/8/4, pointers-first, pointer-typed vs s32+cast fields, 8/C reversed order. Scheduling tie-break never flipped. Suspect the original computes the 0x1E constant some way that makes gcc schedule it before the two %lo adjustments (or the source has an extra no-op statement), or a slightly different field type at unk4/unk8.

